	"data": "The Boring Answer Is the Solarpunk Answer\n\nI went into the solarpunk audit expecting to judge cithoreal's vendor choices. I expected to find hypocrisy — solarpunk values stated, convenience choices made. Instead I found that the vendors (Shelly, Adafruit, Espressif) are surprisingly defensible. The real problem is the power cord.\n\nThe hearth runs on 60% fossil fuel electricity and we never think about it because the wire disappears into the wall. The biggest solarpunk action available is a…",
